  "body": "_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_ | _⚡ Quick win_\n\n**`numbers[0]`/`[1]`과 `numbers[2]`/`[3]` 간의 null-safety 불일치**\n\n`numbers[2]`와 `numbers[3]`에는 `?.length ?? 0`으로 방어 처리가 되어 있지만, `numbers[0]`과 `numbers[1]`은 직접 접근합니다. `numbers`가 `string[]` 타입이라면 배열이 완전히 초기화되지 않은 엣지 케이스에서 `\"undefined\"` 문자가 렌더링될 수 있습니다.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ 수정 제안</summary>\n\n```diff\n- <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[0]}</span>\n- <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[1]}</span>\n+ <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[0] ?? \"\"}</span>\n+ <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[1] ?? \"\"}</span>\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n          <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[0] ?? \"\"}</span>\n          <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>{cardInfo.numbers[1] ?? \"\"}</span>\n          <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>\n            {\"•\".repeat(cardInfo.numbers[2]?.length ?? 0)}\n          </span>\n          <span css={fixedCardNumberStyle}>\n            {\"•\".repeat(cardInfo.numbers[3]?.length ?? 0)}\n          </span>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nVerify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.\n\nIn `@my-app/src/components/Card/Card.tsx` around lines 70 - 77, In the Card\ncomponent render where you output cardInfo.numbers, make the access to\nnumbers[0] and numbers[1] null-safe like you did for numbers[2]/[3]; update the\nspans that reference cardInfo.numbers[0] and cardInfo.numbers[1] (and any other\ndirect index access) to use optional chaining and a fallback (e.g.,\ncardInfo.numbers?.[0] ?? '' or cardInfo.numbers?.[1] ?? '') so you never render\n\"undefined\" — locate the JSX in Card.tsx around the fixedCardNumberStyle spans\nand apply the same defensive pattern to cardInfo.numbers[0]/[1].\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:churro:c09b78ef-93c9-4f69-abc8-a81fe1768067 -->\n\n<!-- 4e71b3a2 -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->",
